// Intel HEX - Hello World! :: RAiNBOW_Hello-World
//   colour     : not assigned by Linguist
//   layer      : full (byte-balanced rainbow bar)
//   upstream   : https://github.com/quxianp/RAiNBOW_Hello-World
//   reference  : see https://esolangs.org/ and https://rosettacode.org/

# Intel HEX, one data record holding "Hello World!".
#
#   :  LL AAAA TT <data> CC
#   |  |  |    |       |__ CC is the two's complement of the
#   |  |  |    |          byte sum, so it must be computed.
#   |  |  |    |____________ twelve bytes: 48 65 6C 6C 6F ...
#   |  |  |_________________ TT = 00, data record
#   |  |____________________ AAAA = 0000, load offset
#   |_______________________ LL = 0C, twelve data bytes
#
# Sum of LL+AAAA+TT+data is 1097 = 0x449, so CC = 0x100-0x49.
:0C00000048656C6C6F20576F726C6421B7
